message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "Rule Engine Core: a declarative complex event processing runtime with deterministic replay and at-least-once delivery"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/rule-engine-core"
url: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/rule-engine-core"
authors:
  - family-names: Ribeiro
    given-names: Diogo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2022-7072"
    email: dfr@esmad.ipp.pt
    affiliation: "ESMAD - School of Media Arts and Design, Polytechnic of Porto"
abstract: >-
  Rule Engine Core is a small, embeddable complex event processing (CEP)
  runtime written in Python. Rules are written declaratively in YAML,
  validated against a formal schema at load time, compiled into executable
  runtime objects, and evaluated deterministically over timestamped,
  entity-keyed event streams. It supports event, window, absence, composite,
  and scheduled triggers, and dispatches emitted alerts through a sink layer
  providing at-least-once delivery with a versioned envelope, deterministic
  idempotency keys, bounded retries, dead-letter recording, and delivery
  metrics.
keywords:
  - complex event processing
  - CEP
  - rule engine
  - declarative rules
  - event stream processing
  - event-time semantics
  - watermark
  - deterministic replay
  - temporal reasoning
  - alerting
  - at-least-once delivery
  - idempotency
  - dead-letter queue
  - observability
  - Python
